Edge overflow of the rolling ball fillet across several faces and on both
sides of the edge, and roundings that overlap on a face between their
edges. On top of 0011: a ball that cannot touch the face beyond a narrow
face may reach a face further on, the contacts on both faces of the edge
may leave them, and two roundings of a face narrower than both run over
it as one.

- ChFi3d_Builder::StartSolOverflow: each side of the section has a support
  that starts as the face of the edge and moves on across the face's edge
  the section crosses between the spine (or the edge it came in by) and
  the contact point, while the contact on the support's surface lies
  beyond such an edge; both sides at once. Where a support's surface has
  no tangent circle with the other side's (a sliver, a face parallel to
  it), the face beyond its edge nearest to the edge it came in by is tried,
  within the ball's diameter; when no face beyond is touched, the side
  rolls on the edge before that face. A side whose contact lies before the
  edge it came in by rolls on that edge (as 0011's obstacle). The start
  touching the faces reached must clear the faces it passed (no face
  nearer to the ball's centre than its radius, ballClears), and the faces
  around those, else that section is not a start (one further along the
  spine may be). The function returns the sides that roll (0, 1 or 2; a
  start rolling on both sides, which touches no face, is not taken: the
  faces are too narrow for the ball on both sides).
- ChFi3d_CutConsumedFaces: the consumed faces between the spine and an
  obstacle edge can be a chain of strips (each with all its vertices on its
  edge toward the obstacle and the edge opposite it), not only one; each
  strip's other edges at the ends of the blend are cut there.
- Roundings that overlap: after the stripes are computed, two stripes
  whose contacts on a face between their edges each lie beyond the other's
  all along (ChFi3d_Builder::OverlappingStripes) are computed again: the
  start of each overflows that face across the other's edge
  (ChFi3d_Builder::OverlapEdge in StartSolOverflow; neither the analytic
  blends nor StartSol are used for them). Both then make the same blend:
  a stripe whose blend lies on another stripe's (the same faces and contact
  curves, ChFi3d_Builder::RemoveCoincidentStripes) stays a contour of the
  builder but gives no faces; the corners are those of the stripes kept.
